{number: 31}
{title: At The Cross}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Alas! And did my Savior bleed?
And [Ab] did my Sovereign [Eb] die?
Would He devote that sacred head
For [Bb7] sinners such as [Eb] I?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
At the [Eb] cross, at the cross
Where I [Bb7] first saw the light,
And the burden of my heart rolled a-[Eb] way,
It was [Ab] there by faith I re-[Eb] ceived my sight,
And now I am [Bb7] happy all the [Eb] day!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Was [Eb] it for crimes that I have done
He [Ab] groaned upon the [Eb] tree?
Amazing pity! Grace unknown!
And [Bb7] love beyond de-[Eb] gree!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Well [Eb] might the sun in darkness hide,
And [Ab] shut his glories [Eb] in,
When Christ, the mighty Maker, died
For [Bb7] man the creature's [Eb] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
But [Eb] drops of grief can ne’er repay
The [Ab] debt of love I [Eb] owe:
Here, Lord, I give my self away,
’Tis [Bb7] all that I can [Eb] do!
{end_of_verse}
